          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: Around July 3, 1993, the owner of a wheat field noticed suspicious traces. The wheat was laid down in large circles connected by straight lines. After investigation, a witness, an architect landscape designer, explained that these were drawings he himself made and provided a step-by-step explanation of the process and method. He was not the author of these circles but the technique used was the same.",
